================================================================================
3. PROJECT ASSUMPTIONS & DESIGN CONSTRAINTS (SRS Section 1.5 & 1.9)
================================================================================
1. Non-Banking Scope:
   In strict accordance with SRS Section 1.5, PennyPal is an educational 
   expense-tracking and budgeting system. It does not connect to real bank 
   accounts or initiate real monetary transfers.
2. Offline-First Resilience:
   Transactions, budgets, cards, and goals are saved immediately to local 
   storage and seamlessly synchronized to Cloud Firestore when an internet 
   connection is detected.
3. Multi-Platform Support:
   A single unified Flutter codebase powers Android smartphones, Android 
   tablets, iOS devices, and desktop/web browsers.
4. AI Multimodal Architecture:
   Uses Google Gemini 3.8 Flash for Receipt OCR and Conversational Advisory, 
   with an automatic deterministic regex/rule-based engine fallback for 
   offline or rate-limited environments.

================================================================================
4. INSTALLATION & SETUP INSTRUCTIONS (MANDATORY)
================================================================================
Prerequisites:
- Flutter SDK >= 3.24.0
- Dart SDK >= 3.5.0
- Java JDK 17
- Android Studio / Android SDK Platform 34

Steps to Run:
1. Extract the project zip file.
2. Open terminal in the project directory:
   cd pennypal
3. Install dependencies:
   flutter pub get
4. Run tests:
   flutter test
5. Launch on device/emulator or Web:
   flutter run -d chrome       (Web browser)
   flutter run -d android      (Android phone/emulator)
6. Build Release APK:
   flutter build apk --split-per-abi

